# Create a clear structure

People skim. They are often standing at a door, holding a phone, with something not working. Put the answer first, then the detail.

## Put the most important thing first

Start with what the person most needs, then add detail. Use short headings that say what the section is for. Do not use “Introduction” or a question as a heading.

| Before | After |
| --- | --- |
| Introduction | Pair a motion sensor |
| How do I reset the hub? | Reset the hub |

<h2 id="wg-050">Order instructions around the task</h2>

Put the step first, then the reason. One action per step, in the order the person does them. After a step that changes something on screen, say what the person should see, so they know it worked.

<%= example('wg-instructions') %>

| Before | After |
| --- | --- |
| Because the hub caches pairing data, you may want to consider restarting it after you have put the sensor into pairing mode by holding the button. | 1. Hold the sensor button for 5 seconds. The light flashes.<br>2. Select **Add device**. The hub starts searching.<br>3. Wait for the sensor to appear in the list. This can take a minute. |

<h2 id="wg-051">State real prerequisites and consequences</h2>

Before a step, say what must already be true. Before a risky step, say what will happen. For a risk to people, see [Write a warning](states-and-errors.html#wg-042).

| Before | After |
| --- | --- |
| Select **Restore**. | Restore replaces everything you have set up since 9 November 2026. Your automations from this week will be lost. Select **Restore** only if you have a backup from today. |
| Update the hub. | The hub must be plugged in and stay on for the whole update. Your lights will not respond for about 5 minutes. |

<h2 id="wg-052">Refer to the actual interface</h2>

Use the label shown on screen, in the order a person meets it. Do not describe a control the screen does not have.

| Before | After |
| --- | --- |
| Use the three-dot menu to disable the automation. | Select **Settings**, then **Automations & scenes**. Turn off the toggle next to **Porch light at sunset**. |
| Click the cog. | Select **Settings**. |

Write “select”, not “click”. Not everyone clicks.

<h2 id="wg-054">Ask only what you need</h2>

Every question must change what happens next. Explain why you are asking, and mark optional questions.

<%= example('wg-form-purpose') %>

| Before | After |
| --- | --- |
| Your full name, date of birth and home address | Name for this household member (optional) |
| Do you want notifications? | Send a notification when the front door opens after 10pm? |

<h2 id="wg-061">Ask for personal information only when needed</h2>

Say why you need it, who sees it and what happens if the person leaves it blank. Never ask for a password or token in a field that does not need one.

| Before | After |
| --- | --- |
| Enter your phone number. | Phone number (optional). Used only to text you when the alarm sounds. |
| Paste your access token here to continue. | Sign in to the manufacturer’s site. civica never asks for your access token. |
